ging for us there's  no doubt about that there's some demands  in there that we find difficult and  people know that we've been discussing  it all through the year about the  challenges that we've got to face up to  they've got a document ready to go  they've shown it to me and they've shown  it to my negotiators and the government  has stopped them putting that document  forward the chief Executives in the  railway know exactly what they've got to  do to make a compromise and demand  compromises off us that's what  negotiations about and Mark Harper is  blocking this I don't think it's him I  think it's the treasury and I think the  hand of Grant sheps is playing a role at  the moment because they share the  documents amongst the Departments and  somebody decided on Sunday night just at  the point of conclusion of these or you  know the next stage of these  negotiations that they had to put driver  on the operation back on table and into  the documents and no matter what you  think of it they know that we can never  accept that as a principle on the  railway and we've been fighting it for  the last six years in various companies  and it's been our policy for 40 years  that we will never accept driver only  operation on our Railway and nor will  driver's Union as lift they've told me  last night that they will never accept  these proposals so when you're in  negotiation you try to find out what the  other side can accept you try to find  out what they can't accept and then you  try and work around those things red  lines and the company is deliberately  throwing uh something that nobody can  accept onto the table when everyone in  our industry even the management the  executive level know that these  negotiations are stuck because of the  attitude of the government okay let's  cut to the chase are you saying that  this government is purposefully  scuppering any chance of a deal  absolutely that's exactly what I'm  saying they have torpedoed the  negotiations and the